# Public-safety gate allow list -- read by scripts/check_public_safe.sh.
#
# One `path:line` per allowed occurrence, with a `#` reason above it. Only
# documentation OF the gate belongs here: a research record that quotes the
# patterns it searched for is evidence, not a leak. Never add a line that
# carries a real credential, path or identity string -- fix that line instead.
#
# `--all` mode reports an entry that no longer matches anything as stale and
# fails, so a doc edit that moves one of these lines is caught rather than
# silently widening the list.

# No entries today. Every file that once quoted the gate's patterns (the scrub
# record and its handoffs and logs) is local-only, so nothing tracked needs an
# exemption. Add an entry only when a tracked document has to quote a pattern.
